{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ecommerce Order & Promotion API",
    "description": "Assessment API examples. Set base_url (no /api suffix), a fresh local customer_email, and a private customer_password (12+ characters with mixed case, a number and symbol; <=72 bytes). Optional ProductSeeder and PromotionSeeder supply demonstration data. This sequence lists stocked products, captures IDs, deletes then re-adds a cart line, applies/removes a promotion, checks out, reads/cancels the order, and logs out. WELCOME10 must be eligible. The first checkout generates a key only when blank; preserve it for retries and clear it for a different purchase. Registration is not repeatable with the same email. On replay after refilling, the old key returns the original order and leaves the cart untouched. Run individual requests as needed. Scripts capture only safe integer IDs; large bigint responses require a lossless JSON client. Credentials and captured tokens must stay local and be cleared before sharing/export. JSON/route/script validation does not mean Postman execution was verified.\n\nBonus 7A: Admin management is a separate folder with its own admin_bearer_token. Register an account locally, run admin:grant for that existing email with APP_ENV=local, then set private admin_email/admin_password and run Admin login. Admin product and promotion creation require unique SKU/code values. PATCH stock_adjustment is an additive, non-idempotent operation; do not blindly rerun it after an uncertain response. No public admin registration or DELETE routes exist.\n\nBonus 7D: All /api endpoints use shared Redis rate limits. Registration: 5/hour/IP. Login: 30/minute/IP, 5/minute/account+IP, 20/minute/account across IPs. Public catalogue and health: 120/minute/IP in separate categories. Customer cart/order/profile reads: 120/minute; cart writes: 60; promotions/logout: 30; checkout/cancellation: 20. Admin reads: 120; admin writes: 30. Authenticated quotas use the stored user, across tokens. A 429 returns error.code TOO_MANY_REQUESTS, error.request_id matching X-Request-ID, Retry-After seconds, X-RateLimit-Limit/Remaining and X-RateLimit-Reset. Respect Retry-After and retain the checkout Idempotency-Key; replays also consume quota. Limiter connection failure is generic 503 before business operations. Never blindly repeat a non-idempotent stock adjustment after an uncertain response. See docs/17-api-rate-limiting.md for proxy, outage and retry trade-offs.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{bearer_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
